{"id": "008d2bf0715d498fbb01ac6aeb0e6b71", "query": "Count ways to fill parking lot with n successive cars of the same make. - description: Given a parking lot of 2n - 2 spaces and 4 car makes, find the number of ways to arrange n successive cars of the same make. - goal: Calculate the total number of arrangements. - constraints: n is between 3 and 30, the parking lot has 2n - 2 spaces, and there are an even number of cars of each make. - generic techniques: Use loops to iterate over the car makes and conditions to handle different cases. - tricky parts: The problem involves finding the number of ways to place?", "raw_text": "?\n---------------------------------------------------\n\n---------------------------------------------------\n===START_JSON===\n{\n  \"explicit_dimensions\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Number_of_cars_per_make\",\n      \"value\": \"even\",\n      \"justification\": \"The user mentions 'an even number of cars of each make' indicating all makes have equal counts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Parking_lot_size\",\n      \"value\": \"2n - 2\",\n      \"justification\": \"Explicit constraint: 'parking lot of 2n - 2 spaces'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Number_of_makes\",\n      \"value\": \"4\",\n      \"justification\": \"The problem describes four car makes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Successive_car_type\",\n      \"value\": \"same_make\",\n      \"justification\": \"Goal is to count arrangements of n successive cars of the same make.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Range_for_n\",\n      \"value\": \"between 3 and 30\",\n      \"justification\": \"Constraints state 'n is between 3 and 30'.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"missed_dimensions\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Edge_cases_for_empty_or_single_car\",\n      \"value\": [\"empty_parking_lot\", \"single_car\"],\n      \"justification\": \"Base cases where n=1 or n=0 affect solution; not discussed in query.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Degenerate_case_where_all_cars_same\",\n      \"value\": \"all_cars_same_make\",\n      \"justification\": \"When all cars have the same make, arrangement reduces to counting rotations; not considered in query.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Data_structure_and_looping_over_permutations\",\n      \"value\": [\"permutations_with_replacement\", \"loops_over_permutations\"],\n      \"justification\": \"Algorithm design depends on permuting the colors or using loops to encode placements; not specified in query.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Rotation_invariance_and_divisibility\",\n      \"value\": [\"divisible_by_n!\", \"rotation_equivalence_classes\"],\n      \"justification\": \"Problem symmetry under rotation implies divisibility by n!; not explicitly discussed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Handling_even_odd_car_counts_and_placement_restrictions\",\n      \"value\": [\"even_count_constraint\", \"odd_count_avoidance\"],\n      \"justification\": \"Placement rules depend on parity of car counts; the query does not fully specify these details.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n===END_JSON===\n\nNote that the output includes both explicit dimensions (directly stated or implied) and missed dimensions (important aspects not mentioned in the original query). These missed dimensions are intended to guide further discussion and refinement of the solution approach.", "json_data": {"explicit_dimensions": [{"name": "Number_of_cars_per_make", "value": "even", "justification": "The user mentions 'an even number of cars of each make' indicating all makes have equal counts."}, {"name": "Parking_lot_size", "value": "2n - 2", "justification": "Explicit constraint: 'parking lot of 2n - 2 spaces'."}, {"name": "Number_of_makes", "value": "4", "justification": "The problem describes four car makes."}, {"name": "Successive_car_type", "value": "same_make", "justification": "Goal is to count arrangements of n successive cars of the same make."}, {"name": "Range_for_n", "value": "between 3 and 30", "justification": "Constraints state 'n is between 3 and 30'."}], "implicit_dimensions": [{"name": "Edge_cases_for_empty_or_single_car", "value": ["empty_parking_lot", "single_car"], "justification": "Base cases where n=1 or n=0 affect solution; not discussed in query."}, {"name": "Degenerate_case_where_all_cars_same", "value": "all_cars_same_make", "justification": "When all cars have the same make, arrangement reduces to counting rotations; not considered in query."}, {"name": "Data_structure_and_looping_over_permutations", "value": ["permutations_with_replacement", "loops_over_permutations"], "justification": "Algorithm design depends on permuting the colors or using loops to encode placements; not specified in query."}, {"name": "Rotation_invariance_and_divisibility", "value": ["divisible_by_n!", "rotation_equivalence_classes"], "justification": "Problem symmetry under rotation implies divisibility by n!; not explicitly discussed."}, {"name": "Handling_even_odd_car_counts_and_placement_restrictions", "value": ["even_count_constraint", "odd_count_avoidance"], "justification": "Placement rules depend on parity of car counts; the query does not fully specify these details."}]}, "logprobs": [-5.265826225280762, -0.588705837726593, -0.6705841422080994, -3.005993127822876, -0.04555078595876694, -1.6526802778244019, -0.0012734169140458107, -0.0004991239402443171, -0.0072801304049789906, -0.000898077036254108, -0.0030043248552829027, -7.510157047363464e-06, -4.124556289752945e-05, -0.0003692421887535602, -0.001342110801488161, -0.0003491030656732619, -0.0023436478804796934, -0.02085413597524166, -0.00014733182615600526, -1.8000440832111053e-05, -1.3351351299206726e-05, -0.00010418349120300263, -0.0005738280597142875, -2.5453343391418457, -3.0528602600097656, -0.34038323163986206, -0.0023934785276651382, -0.8158416152000427, -0.09075765311717987, -0.20216098427772522, -5.8412379075889476e-06, -2.861018856492592e-06, -1.0013530300057027e-05, -3.9934315282152966e-05, -0.04796450957655907, -1.2920575141